# Deploy target: ck6filter

Going forward, ship product changes to the **ck6filter@cavinkare.com** stack:

- **GitHub (source of truth):** `https://github.com/6Filter/6-Filter-Test.git` (remote `origin`, branch `main`)
- **GitHub (Render deploy mirror, public):** `https://github.com/cavinkarecia/6-Filter-Test-ck6filter` (remote `ck6filter-deploy`) — used because ck6filter Render cannot yet fetch the private `6Filter` org repo
- **Render account / workspace:** logged in as `ck6filter@cavinkare.com` (`tea-dbta5et6e07s73bsi9t0`)
- **Web service:** `ck-6-filter-test` (`srv-dbtckp67bikc73dnujvg`) → https://ck-6-filter-test-88wu.onrender.com
- **Postgres:** `6-Filter-Test-Live` (`dpg-dbtca9rbc2fs73doghpg-a`)
- **Build / start:** `npm ci --include=dev && npm run build` / `npm start`

## Workflow after meaningful code changes

1. Commit (when the user asks, or when they asked to push/deploy).
2. `git push origin HEAD` (pre-push runs `ciDryRun`; fix real failures, do not `--no-verify`).
3. Sync the public deploy mirror (omit `.github/workflows` if the OAuth token lacks `workflow` scope), then ensure Render points at that mirror on `main`.
4. If auto-deploy does not fire: `render services update srv-dbtckp67bikc73dnujvg --build-command "…" --start-command "npm start" --confirm` then `render deploys create srv-dbtckp67bikc73dnujvg --confirm`.

## Preferred long-term fix

Connect the **ck6filter** Render GitHub App to the private `6Filter` org, then retarget the service to `https://github.com/6Filter/6-Filter-Test` and retire the public mirror.

Do not print Render API keys or database URLs.
